fix(agent): stop reflexive tool-rummaging on plain chat + clean list_files error

Mason's screenshot: a purely conversational message ("I prefer dark roast,
I decided $20, help me plan the launch") triggered list_files, github_list_prs,
read_file, and more list_files — none of which the message asked for. The
agent treated every turn as "go explore the folder/tools."

- AGENT_SYSTEM rewritten: tools are OPTIONAL, use ONLY when the request needs
  one; if the user is chatting/sharing/asking-answerable, JUST REPLY — never
  read/list files or call an API speculatively "to gather context"; prefer the
  fewest tool calls. (Prompt nudge, not a hard guarantee — watch for recurrence.)
- list_files on a FILE now returns clean guidance ("'X' is a file, not a
  directory. Use read_file...") instead of the raw "Not a directory (os error
  20)". Empty dir returns "(empty directory)". File-op errors read like help,
  not OS noise.
